Seventh planning pass B/2 — static SPIDR shards, execution budgets, DoD trace and QA rejection bar. Continues comment-6a39659a.

DO NOT BUILD TWO GIANT FAULT FILES
The earlier F1/F2 sketches are too broad once production catalogs land. Preserve every boundary’s BEFORE/AFTER/RACE family together, but split by responsibility. Current planning floor (must be recomputed/pinned from the final production catalogs; it may rise and never silently shrink):
- transaction/WAL 24;
- outbox/adversity 24;
- activation/process 24;
- provider stream/cancel 20;
- resource 16;
- budget 18;
- artifact stage/persist 16;
- artifact verify/delete 12.
That is 154 production fault cases, plus harness/security self-tests, existing Foundation entries, and delegated Linux/macOS/restore sets.

Static task DAG, each <=5 files and <=8 steps:
H0 common protocol/evidence/child runner (5 files);
S0 store worker+harness+self-test (3);
S1 transaction/WAL cases+matrix (2);
S2 outbox/adversity cases+matrix (2);
R0 runtime worker+real fixture-provider+harness+self-test (4);
R1 activation/process (2);
R2 provider stream/cancel (2);
R3 resource (2);
R4 budget (2);
R5 artifact stage/persist (2);
R6 artifact verify/delete (2);
P final fault coverage/adversarial aggregate (2).
Support-only tasks name their first real consumer. Never split by arbitrary case index, seed, platform conditional or phase. P asserts shard union equals the production obligation set, intersections empty, every shard count >0, generated=started=completed and every shardId frozen. Linux/macOS/restore stay with existing owners.

Split again before approval if a slice exceeds 5 files, 8 steps, 32 process-spawning cases, ~60 minutes human work, or ~300 test lines. If a complete focused command exceeds 180s twice on the same host (provider/cancel ceiling 240s), split by subsystem/boundary and still run every case. Never sample, use dynamic --shard, reduce seeds in CI, or omit a phase.

FAULT LANE EXECUTION
Dedicated config must set passWithNoTests:false, bail:0, fileParallelism:false, maxWorkers:1 and sequence.concurrent:false; forbid .concurrent/retry/skip/todo/skipIf/runIf. One normal child at a time; exactly two only inside an authored RACE. CI may parallelize static shard files only on separate clean runners, but completion pnpm test:fault runs all serially.

Timeouts: READY 5s; ordinary case 15s; hang/cancel uses exported production deadline +5s capped at 30s (no exported bounded deadline is a prerequisite); cleanup 10s; per-case Vitest 40s; hook 15s. H0’s intentional hang self-test uses a 250ms local harness. Stdout/stderr <=64KiB. Timeout/overflow/protocol/cleanup uncertainty is HARNESS_INVALID/FAIL, never product UNKNOWN. afterEach terminates through production platform observation, closes handles/DBs, proves no stale lock by reopen, and deletes only a resolved descendant of the case temp root; afterAll emergency-cleans leaks and keeps the shard red.

Exact focused command pattern for every shard:
pnpm exec tsc -p tests/fault/tsconfig.json && pnpm exec vitest run --config tests/fault/vitest.config.ts <one exact *.fault.ts file>
Use exact files:
tests/fault/harness/harness-selftest.fault.ts;
tests/fault/store/store-harness-selftest.fault.ts;
transaction-wal-matrix.fault.ts;
outbox-adversity-matrix.fault.ts;
tests/fault/runtime/runtime-harness-selftest.fault.ts;
activation-process-matrix.fault.ts;
provider-stream-matrix.fault.ts;
resource-matrix.fault.ts;
budget-matrix.fault.ts;
artifact-stage-matrix.fault.ts;
artifact-verify-delete-matrix.fault.ts.
These are development gates. P uses only the exact full task command.

MECHANICAL DoD TRACE
DoD1:
- nonempty distribution components = public-root catalogs = generated = executed;
- every AUTHORITY/EXTERNAL_EFFECT row has exact (boundary,fault,BEFORE|AFTER|RACE) equality;
- every subject has public root, non-test consumer, observation entry and same-basis record;
- schedule manifest has no unmapped/unhit obligation and nonzero counts.

DoD2:
- refused rows have zero unauthorized delta except exact declared audit/no-effect/replay-claim cardinality;
- one effect identity has <=1 provider invocation; replay returns identical decision/result/effect and adds nothing;
- budget is conserved, capacity bounded, UNKNOWN never funds work;
- AST has no skip family; declared=generated=executed>0; unreadable/abort is explicit and red/UNKNOWN, never omission;
- false/corrupt/tampered/cross-basis evidence never gains authority;
- every negative row asserts source component+stage+layer+code and intended compile-valid mutants all die.

DoD3:
- every host row has independent assertion verdict, production truth, scope disposition, exact reason and scopeRef;
- OUTSIDE_SCOPE whitelist is design-exact and host-malicious only;
- unsupported/unavailable host is IN_SCOPE+UNKNOWN;
- UNKNOWN/outside are printed separately and excluded from positive claim count; UNKNOWN->PASS mutation reds.

DoD4:
- lane scripts run strict recursive tsc plus dedicated serial Vitest configs with nonzero discovery;
- fresh exact command exits 0 and prints source/catalog/case/evidence digests and separate FAIL/UNKNOWN/outside counts;
- evidence validates and redaction scan is zero leaks with planted count >0.

CLAIM AGGREGATION
Encode FAIL > UNKNOWN > PASS, not prose. A verified invariant breach/code-layer mismatch/tamper acceptance is FAIL even when other evidence is missing. UNKNOWN applies only when no known breach exists and required evidence is missing/partial/unreadable/cross-basis/unverifiable. PASS requires every permit-list predicate complete at one basis. OUTSIDE_SCOPE is a separate disposition, never a PASS truth claim. The task’s own engineering evidence never licenses any public benchmark sentence.

QA MUST REJECT THE FUTURE PLAN if any is true:
- prerequisite/public root/consumer/observer/adapter/lane/mutation capability absent or not DONE;
- mock/helper/deep import or test-authored central boundary universe substitutes for production;
- owner row missing/duplicate or path collision unresolved;
- no exact component/catalog/generated/executed equality or any zero/filtered dimension;
- return-value/spy-only proof, open-ended deltas, code without layer/stage, or mapped inner refusal flattened to UNKNOWN_ERROR;
- replay/effect/budget/resource/evidence/redaction/GO separation lacks an independent oracle;
- UNKNOWN can mask FAIL, OUTSIDE_SCOPE is runtime-selected/unsupported-host/PASS, or positive counts include either;
- evidence mixes commits, includes volatile identity/secrets/paths, or is committed;
- confirmatory corpus is touched by this task;
- hidden skip/early return/zero cases can stay green;
- mutation uses helper, accepts compile/unrelated failure, lacks named kill ids, survives, or edits shared unowned paths without the approved isolated runner/amendment;
- final verification differs from pnpm test:fault && pnpm test:security, is stale/filtered, or ordinary-root leakage/zero discovery exists.

Post-implementation reject on any set/digest mismatch, zero count, hidden skip, wrong code/layer/stage/audit, canary leak, unauthorized delta, duplicate invocation, mint/capacity breach, false evidence acceptance, UNKNOWN inflation, surviving mutant, mixed basis, generated committed artifact, pinned-hash mismatch, or nonzero/zero-discovery final leg.

